From c1d1e941b700ff565f5de3b9f48f0bf925e9e94d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:57:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Strict index.json: NaN / Infinity in the alerts report become
 null (PR #90 option A)

The validation block's empty "today" / "this week" figures carried NaN since
ef6620013. The browser's JSON.parse rejects NaN, so the site lost the whole alerts
block of index.json on days with nothing decided: every alert card stayed empty.
notify.run now returns its report through notify.json_safe. site/app.js getJSON
also reads bare NaN / Infinity as null, for files written before the fix.

Infrastructure only: phone alerts, plans, the registered tests and the freeze key
are unchanged. A replay of 3 days of real data gives identical phone messages
(55 messages, 484 lines), report, state and store files; only NaN becomes null.
Test: tests/test_index_json_strict.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9BUECqqTrTgQY1HRzyrvM
